        "## TASK 1 – Discourse and the Unit of Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "### Theoretical Foundations\n",
        "- **Discourse**: A coherent structured sequence of linguistic utterances longer than a single sentence.\n",
        "- **Discourse Segment**: A functional unit of discourse consisting of one or more utterances that exhibit local structural, topical, or intentional cohesion.\n",
        "- **Utterance**: The physical realization of a linguistic act bounded by silence or turn changes.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Processing sentences independently vs. in a Discourse Context\n",
        "*Example from our corpus:*\n",
        "1. *\"The road in Sector 4 is flooded.\"*\n",
        "2. *\"It is completely blocked.\"*\n",
        "\n",
        "If processed independently, an information extraction pipeline cannot resolve the reference \"It\" in the second sentence. The control room misses crucial spatial-situational mapping because it cannot connect \"blocked\" to \"the road in Sector 4\".\n",
        "\n",
        "### Report Segmentation Criteria\n",
        "Segmentation utilizes distinct markers:\n",
        "1. **Cue phrases**: Words like \"At the same time\", \"However\", \"Then\".\n",
        "2. **Tense shifts**: Transitioning from past to present/future signals a boundaries.\n",
        "3. **Topic transitions**: Shifting from \"road closure\" to \"power failure\" indicates segment boundaries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "a4d8ec4d",
        "outputId": "b7c3b48a-a958-460b-cd32-f6ba779eb9e0"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Demonstration of Discourse Unit Segmentation\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "sample_thread = \"The road in Sector 4 is flooded. It is completely blocked. Avoid this route. At the same time, power lines are down in Sector 2.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "def discourse_segmenter(text):\n",
        "    # Segmenting on sentence boundaries and cue phrases\n",
        "    raw_sentences = text.split(\". \")\n",
        "    segmented = []\n",
        "    for sentence in raw_sentences:\n",
        "        stripped = sentence.strip().rstrip(\".\")\n",
        "        if \"At the same time\" in stripped:\n",
        "            parts = stripped.split(\"At the same time\")\n",
        "            segmented.append(parts[0].strip())\n",
        "            segmented.append(\"At the same time\" + parts[1])\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            segmented.append(stripped)\n",
        "    return [s for s in segmented if s]\n",
        "\n",
        "segments = discourse_segmenter(sample_thread)\n",
        "for idx, seg in enumerate(segments):\n",
        "    print(f\"Segment {idx+1}: {seg}\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Segment 1: The road in Sector 4 is flooded\n",
            "Segment 2: It is completely blocked\n",
            "Segment 3: Avoid this route\n",
            "Segment 4: At the same time, power lines are down in Sector 2\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
