        "## TASK 2 – Reference Resolution (Hobbs & Centering)\n",
        "\n",
        "### Theoretical Context\n",
        "- **Anaphora**: A linguistic expression (e.g., pronoun) that refers back to an entity introduced earlier in the discourse (the antecedent).\n",
        "- **Cataphora**: A linguistic expression referring forward to an antecedent that appears later.\n",
        "- **Antecedent**: The entity/noun-phrase to which an anaphor refers.\n",
        "- **Discourse Referent**: A mental representations of entities introduced and maintained across the discourse model.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Classification of Referring Expressions\n",
        "1. **Pronoun**: \"It\", \"They\"\n",
        "2. **Definite Noun Phrase**: \"The flooded road\"\n",
        "3. **Proper Name**: \"High Street\"\n",
        "4. **Demonstrative**: \"This route\""
      ]
